- ## Smart Timing Logic
- When `-SmartTiming` is enabled:
- 1. Reads cron jobs from ~/.openclaw/cron/jobs.json
- 2. Parses all schedule types (cron, every, at)
- 3. Checks next scheduled task times
- 4. Only proceeds if no task in next $CronLookAhead minutes
- 5. Checks system idle time using Windows API
- 6. Only proceeds if idle > threshold
- 7. Retries check every minute until conditions met
- 8. Max wait time: $MaxWait minutes (then proceeds anyway)
- ## What It Does
- 1. Auto-detects gateway port from config
- 2. Analyzes cron schedules to avoid user task windows
- 3. Optionally waits for system idle (smart timing)
- 4. Checks OpenClaw core version vs latest npm
- 5. Checks installed skills for updates via clawhub
- 6. Performs AI impact assessment
- 7. If High risk: pause and request approval
- 8. Sends pre-update notification (if not -NoNotify)
- 9. Performs updates if approved (with -AutoUpdate)
- 10. Restarts gateway after update
- 11. Verifies gateway health is restored
- 12. Sends completion notification
- ## Updates Both
- - **OpenClaw Core**: Via `npm update -g openclaw`
- - **Installed Skills**: Via `clawhub update --all`
